Did you rub a lamp you didn't know was blessed? If so, _don't ever do
that_!

Did you rub a known-blessed lamp you weren't sure was magic? That's
not necessarily a bad thing to do, but the wish shouldn't have been a
big surprise.

(When you find a lamp, #name the item type. If you find another lamp
which doesn't take the name, you know one of the two is magic. If you
have four lamps and three of them are the same item type, odds are
that the odd one out is magic. Also, is a lamp runs out of oil, you
know it's not a magic one.)

> I don't know what to wish for.

AOL to the other posters suggesting GDSM. Yes, SDSM+CoMR is modestly
better in the long term, but you need to live long enough to get
there, and lack of MR is quickly deadly. (Without it, all it takes is
one polytrap to wreck all your armor, for starters.)

GDSM fixes what may be your two worst problems: lack of MR and lousy
AC. (To some extent, better AC can help offset things like not having
a top-shelf weapon and not being very fast.)

You've got a lot of good gear already. Use this wish to keep yourself
alive to the castle wand, whereupon you'll likely be able to kit
yourself out any way you like.

